    "body": "Read-only check on a comparable Windows 11 box (the reporter's mini PC: AMD Ryzen 5 7640HS, onboard **Radeon 760M**, 2 GB UMA frame buffer, 2x16 GB DDR5 at its rated 4800 MT/s, no memory overclock). No freeze was attempted.\n\n- **21 days of System event logs:** no unexpected shutdown (Kernel-Power 41 / EventLog 6008), no bugcheck (1001), and **no display-driver timeout or reset** (Display 4101 / amdkmdag / dxgkrnl).\n- In that period the box ran CamCraft's full Windows quick gate many times, including the GPU UI suites (wgpu on the Radeon), all green.\n- Graphics driver here: 32.0.12033.1030 (dated 2024-11-26).\n\n**Reading:** CamCraft's GPU use does not freeze this Ryzen + onboard Radeon class of machine in general, which points at the reporter's PC: the driver version and/or memory stability (snow, then a lock-up, also with local AI apps, matches integrated-GPU memory trouble, e.g. XMP/EXPO overclock or a too-small UMA buffer). The questions already asked (dxdiag, XMP off, UMA 2-4 GB, the current AMD driver, OCCT/MemTest86) remain the way to confirm. A software-renderer fallback switch (see #2423) is the safe workaround meanwhile.\n\nNext: if the reporter answers, compare their driver date and memory settings with the above.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
